    <statement><p>Compute the length of the curve <m>{\bf r\it(t)} = \left\lt 2t,\ln t ,t^2\right&gt;</m> over the interval <m>1 \le t \le 5</m></p>
<p><m>L=</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>25.6094</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>\bf r\it(t)</m> is <m>\bf r\it'(t)=\left\lt 2,\frac{1}{t},2t\right&gt;</m>. We use the Arc Length Formula to obtain:
<me>L=\int_1^{5}\|\bf r\it'(t)\|\,dt=
\int_1^{5}\sqrt{2^2+\left(\frac{1}{t}\right)^2 +(2t)^2}\,dt</me>



<me>=\int_1^{5}\sqrt{\left(2t + \frac{1}{t}\right)^2}\,dt = 
\left.\int_1^{5}\left(2t + \frac{1}{t}\right)\,dt =
t^2 + \ln t\right|_1^{5}</me>



<me>=\left(25+\ln 5\right) - (1+ \ln 1) = 24+\ln 5</me>



</solution>
